Capsule's fix for SDL 3.4.18's joystick hotplug stall on Windows. Every HID device arrival or removal made
the next joystick update rescan DirectInput's game controllers on the thread that updates joysticks:
IDirectInput8_EnumDevices creates and queries each device, 100 ms and more, up to three times a plug (the
change, then the 300 ms and 2 s timers). The joystick thread now runs that scan with a DirectInput object of
its own, and the detect merges the scan once it lands, holding the device list as it stands until then. The
first detect at init still scans synchronously, and the detect scans itself whenever the thread cannot. Drop
it once SDL releases a fix (libsdl-org/SDL#15403).

